          <p style="margin-top: 5em;">
          </p><h4 class="action">WEATHER FOR THE BLIND</h4><br>

<!-- PLAYER WIDGET CODE -->
<h4>PRESS PLAY BELOW TO HEAR LIVE STREAM FROM NEW ORLEANS</h4><p></p>
<h5>Listen Live: (allow a few seconds for audio to start)</h5>
<p><audio controls="controls" preload="none">
  <source src="https://audio.wavefarm.org/weatherwarlock.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
  Please update your browser to the latest version. This player should work in all current versions of Chrome, Firefox, Safari and IE.
</audio></p>
<h5>Or, listen to this sample recording:</h5>
<p><audio controls="controls" preload="none">
  <source src="https://data.wavefarm.org/20230620092841/weatherwarlock_soundsamples.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
</audio></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">If the New Orleans station is off-air, please link to our <a href="https://wavefarm.org/ta/archive/works/g7yqrm" target="_blank">UPSTATE NY LIVE STREAM</a></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Weather for the blind is a live streaming site of a musical instrument which is played by the weather. The base station –<a href="/static/img/warlock.jpg" target="_blank"> pictured in the foreground</a> – is called Weather Warlock and is currently streaming live from New Orleans. In the event that the home stream is down, you can check out the live stream of our “Upstate Warlock”, stationed at <a title="Wave Farm Weather Warlock" href="http://wavefarm.org/ta/works/g7yqrm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wave Farm</a> in Acra New York.</p>
<p>The weather sensors – <a href="/static/img/sensors-close.jpg" target="_blank">pictured in the distant surf</a> – are mounted to a post and detect temperature, wind-speed, UV index, barometric pressure, flooding, and atmospheric moisture. This all-analog synthesizer produces a wide range of tones and harmonics based around a consonant B flat major chord with special audio events occurring during sunrise and sunset. A new companion-instrument called, “Traffic Saxx” is also mixed into the stream. Traffic Saxx captures and filters the white noise from traffic on St. Claude Avenue, changing a sound which can be stressful, into something more oceanic and calming. Weather Warlock evolved from an earlier incarnation called “Weather Witch”, developed by Mars Brown and Quintron. The very first prototype was called&nbsp;“Singing House” which was debuted by N.O. Airlift in 2011.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<br><br>
<h4>CURRENT LOCATION: NEW ORLEANS, LA</h4>
